6498438 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186497887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186497979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186497887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a7d01b58-0857-54fb-bdf6-61d33e711eeb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498590 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498590 #edb/ref 1069 "q-126851" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498590 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498590 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e9/e9892ef4efa3481ad02f7b8e38f1bae1876b196627204521d011656010297281.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=16,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=6,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=4,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ is oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of ${∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498590 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2260d96-b984-5295-801c-28a9593008a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498590 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/b2/b20b2b911c2a417c26fa951d9b28efa296c265df25e9d06b635ef4846267b93b.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =16+6+4 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498611 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498611 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1b31cf93-d5e4-581a-abf0-1f4ce4b0318a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498611 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186369434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498614 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498614 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2056fd1b-d5a8-5347-8cd3-9a0ecc4618d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498614 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186369462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498629 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498629 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6fb02394-525d-5f30-9775-578f4448db13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498629 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498640 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "96ebff15-a11c-5705-a99b-83a08193b653" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498640 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186498490 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498650 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498650 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c3cbee15-50e1-5853-bd12-2ab6e6059abb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498650 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186498590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186519610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186519631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186519647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921865